\sa200\par\trowd\trleft960\trhdr \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx3760\clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx6560\clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \b\fs20\f1 Variable\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \b\fs20\f1 Value\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \b\fs20\f1 Description\sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx3760\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx6560\clvertalb\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 host (m)\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 ip\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  SMSC Host name or IP \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 port (m)\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 port number\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  SMSC Port number \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 receive-port (m)\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 port number\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  The port in which the SMSC will contact \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 ois-debug-level\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 number 0 to 8\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  extra debug, optional, see smsc_ois.c \sa60\cell \row \pard\plain\sl-1\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb200\li960\sl234 \fs18\f2 \sa0\par\fi0\sb0
group = smsc\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
smsc = oisd\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
host = 103.102.101.100\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
port = 10000\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
keepalive = 25\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
my-number = 12345\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
validityperiod = 30\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
\sa200\par\trowd\trleft960\trhdr \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx3760\clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx6560\clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \b\fs20\f1 Variable\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \b\fs20\f1 Value\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \b\fs20\f1 Description\sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx3760\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx6560\clvertalb\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 host (m)\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 ip\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  SMSC Host name or IP \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 port (m)\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 port number\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  SMSC Port number \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 keepalive\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 number\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  SMSC connection will not be left idle for longer than this many seconds. The right value to use depends on how eager the SMSC is to close idle connections. If you see many unexplained reconnects, try lowering this value. Set it to 0 to disable this feature. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 my-number\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 string\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Any valid SME number acceptable by SMSC. This number is used only in keepalive request. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 validityperiod\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 integer\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  How long the message will be valid, i.e., how long the SMS center (the real one, not the phone acting as one for Kannel) will try to send the message to the recipient. Defined in minutes. \sa60\cell \row \pard\plain\sl-1\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb216\s3\li960\sl374 {\*\bkmkstart _2272}{\*\bkmkend _2272}\b\fs28\f1 SM/ASI (for CriticalPath InVoke SMS Center 4.x)\keepn\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb144\li960\sl260 \b0\fs20\lang1033\f0 This implements Short Message/Advanced Service Interface (SM/ASI) Protocol for the use of connecting to a CriticalPath InVoke SMS Center. Sample configuration:\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb200\li960\sl234 \fs18\lang1024\f2 \sa0\par\fi0\sb0
group = smsc\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
smsc = smasi\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
host = 10.11.12.13\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
port = 23456\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
smsc-username = foo\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
smsc-password = foo\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
\sa200\par\trowd\trleft960\trhdr \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx3760\clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx6560\clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \b\fs20\f1 Variable\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \b\fs20\f1 Value\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \b\fs20\f1 Description\sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx3760\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx6560\clvertalb\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 host (m)\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 hostname\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Machine that runs SMSC. As IP (10.11.12.13) or hostname (host.foobar.com) \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 port (m)\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 port-number\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  The port number for the connection to the SMSC. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 smsc-username (m)\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 string\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  The 'username' of the Messaging Entity connecting to the SMSC. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 smsc-password (m)\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 string\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  The password matching the "smsc-username" your teleoperator provided you with. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 reconnect-delay\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 number\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Optional, the time between attempts to connect to an SMSC having failed to connect initiating or during an session. The default is 10 seconds. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 source-addr-ton\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 number\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Optional, source address TON setting for the link. (Defaults to 1). \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 source-addr-npi\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 number\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Optional, source address NPI setting for the link. (Defaults to 1). \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 dest-addr-ton\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 number\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Optional, destination address TON setting for the link. (Defaults to 1). \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 dest-addr-npi\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 number\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Optional, destination address NPI setting for the link. (Defaults to 1). \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 priority\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 number\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Optional, sets the default priority of messages transmitted over this smsc link. (Defaults to 0, which is the lowest priority). \sa60\cell \row \pard\plain\sl-1\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb216\s3\li960\sl374 {\*\bkmkstart _2344}{\*\bkmkend _2344}\b\fs28\f1 GSM modem\keepn\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb200\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw40\brsp100\li1600\ri200\brdrl\brdrs\brdrw40\brsp200\li1600\ri200\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw40\brsp0\li1600\ri200\brdrr\brdrs\brdrw40\brsp200\li1600\ri200\sl374\qc Warning\keepn\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb100\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw40\brsp100\li1600\ri200\brdrl\brdrs\brdrw40\brsp200\li1600\ri200\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw40\brsp0\li1600\ri200\brdrr\brdrs\brdrw40\brsp200\li1600\ri200\sl234 \b0\fs18\lang1033 See {\field{\*\fldinst   HYPERLINK  \\l ID_upgrading_45_notes}{\fldrslt Appendix A}} for changes.\keepn\hyphpar0\par\pard\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw40\brsp100\li1600\ri200\brdrl\brdrs\brdrw40\brsp200\li1600\ri200\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw40\brsp0\li1600\ri200\brdrr\brdrs\brdrw40\brsp200\li1600\ri200\sl-100\keepn\par\pard\sl-1\par\pard\sb200\li960\sl260 \fs20\f0 This driver allows a GSM Modem or Phone to be connected to Kannel and work as a virtual SMSC\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb200\li960\sl234 \fs18\lang1024\f2 \sa0\par\fi0\sb0
group = smsc\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
smsc = at\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
modemtype = auto\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
device = /dev/ttyS0\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
speed = 9600\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
pin = 2345\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
\sa200\par\trowd\trleft960\trhdr \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx3760\clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx6560\clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \b\fs20\f1 Variable\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \b\fs20\f1 Value\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \b\fs20\f1 Description\sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx3760\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx6560\clvertalb\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 modemtype\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 string\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Modems from different manufacturers have slightly different behavior. We need to know what type of modem is used. Use "auto" or omit parameter to have Kannel detect the modem type automatically. (some types should not be auto-detected like the Nokia Premicell). \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 device (m)\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 device-name\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  The device the modem is connected to, like \fs18\f2 /dev/ttyS0\fs20\f0 . When the device name is set to \fs18\f2 rawtcp\fs20\f0  or \fs18\f2 telnet\fs20\f0  two other variables are required in the configuration: \fs18\f2 host\fs20\f0  and \fs18\f2 port\fs20\f0 . See the note below. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 speed\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 serial speed in bps\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  The speed in bits per second. Default value 0 means to try to use speed from modem definition, or if it fails, try to autodetect. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 pin\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 string\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  This is the PIN number of the SIM card in the GSM modem. You can specify this option if your SIM has never been used before and needs to have the PIN number entered. The PIN is usually a four digit number. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 validityperiod\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 integer\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  How long the message will be valid, i.e., how long the SMS center (the real one, not the phone acting as one for Kannel) will try to send the message to the recipient. Encoded as per the GSM 03.40 standard, section 9.2.3.12. Default is 167, meaning 24 hours. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 keepalive\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 seconds\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Kannel would "ping" the modem for this many seconds. If the probe fails, try to reconnect to it. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 my-number\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 number\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Optional phone number. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 sms-center\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 number\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  SMS Center to send messages. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 sim-buffering\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 boolean\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Whether to enable the so-called "SIM buffering behavior" of the GSM module. if assigned a true value, the module will query the message storage memory of the modem and will process and delete any messages found there. this does not alter normal behavior, but only add the capability of reading messages that were stored in the memory for some reason. The type of memory to use can be selected using the 'message-storage' parameter of the modem configuration. Polling the memory is done at the same interval as keepalive (if set) or 60 seconds (if not set). NOTE: This behavior is known to cause minor or major hiccups for a few buggy modems. Modems known to work with this setting are Wavecom WM02/M1200 and the Siemens M20. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 max-error-count\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 integer\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Maximal error count for opening modem device or initializing of the modem before \fs18\f2 reset-string\fs20\f0  will be executed. This is useful when modem crashed and needs hard reset. Default disabled. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 host\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 IP address\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Hostname or IP address to connect in \fs18\f2 rawtcp\fs20\f0  mode. Required if \fs18\f2 device\fs20\f0  is set to \fs18\f2 rawtcp\fs20\f0 . \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 port\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 integer\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  TCP port to connect to on \fs18\f2 rawtcp-host\fs20\f0 . Required if \fs18\f2 device\fs20\f0  is set to \fs18\f2 rawtcp\fs20\f0 . \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 smsc-username\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 string\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Username to use on a Login: or User: prompt prior to be connected to the modem. Useful if modem is connected to a terminal server and \fs18\f2 rawtcp\fs20\f0  mode or \fs18\f2 telnet\fs20\f0  mode are used. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 smsc-password\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 string\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Username to use on a Password prompt prior to be connected to the modem. Useful if modem is connected to a terminal server and \fs18\f2 rawtcp\fs20\f0  mode or \fs18\f2 telnet\fs20\f0  mode are used. \fs18\f2 smsc-password\fs20\f0  can be used alone without \fs18\f2 smsc-username\fs20\f0  for devices only asking for a password. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 login-prompt\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 string\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  An alternative string to be used instead of Login: or Username: \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 password-prompt\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 string\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  An alternative string to be used instead of Password: \sa60\cell \row \pard\plain\sl-1\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb200\li960\sl260 \fs20\lang1033 Modem definitions are now multiple groups present in kannel.conf, either directly or, for example, by including the example modems.conf. (See {\field{\*\fldinst   HYPERLINK  \\l ID_includes_46_title}{\fldrslt \i Inclusion of configuration files}})\sa200\par\trowd\trleft960\trhdr \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx3760\clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx6560\clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \b\fs20\f1 Variable\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \b\fs20\f1 Value\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \b\fs20\f1 Description\sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx3760\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx6560\clvertalb\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 group\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 modems\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  This is a mandatory variable \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 id\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 string\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  This is the the id that should be used in \fs18\f2 modemtype\fs20\f0  variable from AT2 \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 name\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 string\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  The name of this modem configuration. Used in logs \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 detect-string\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 string\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  String to use when trying to detect the modem. See \fs18\f2 detect-string2\fs20\f0  \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 detect-string2\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 string\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Second string to use to detect the modem. For example, if the modem replies with "SIEMENS MODEM M20", \fs18\f2 detect-string\fs20\f0  could be "SIEMENS" and \fs18\f2 detect-string2\fs20\f0  "M20" \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 init-string\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 string\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Optional initialization string. Defaults to "AT+CNMI=1,2,0,1,0" \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 speed\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 number\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Serial port hint speed to use. Optional. Defaults to smsc group speed or autodetect \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 enable-hwhs\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 string\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Optional AT command to enable hardware handshake. Defaults to "AT+IFC=2,2" \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 hardware-flow-control\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 boolean\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Optionally disable hardware handshake on the computer side by setting it to false. Defaults to true. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 need-sleep\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 boolean\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Optional. Defaults to false. Some modems needs to sleep after opening the serial port and before first command \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 no-pin\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 boolean\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Optional. Defaults to false. If the modem doesn't support the PIN command, enable this \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 no-smsc\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 boolean\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Optional. Defaults to false. If the modem doesn't support setting the SMSC directly on the PDU, enable this. (Default is to include a "00" at the beginning of the PDU to say it's the default smsc, and remove the "00" when receiving) \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 sendline-sleep\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 number (milliseconds)\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Optional, defaults to 100 milliseconds. The sleep time after sending a AT command. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 keepalive-cmd\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 string\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Optional, defaults to "AT". If keepalive is activated in AT2 group, this is the command to be sent. If your modem supports it, for example, use "AT+CBC;+CSQ", and see in logs the reply "+CBC: 0,64" (0=On battery, 64% full) and "+CSQ: 14,99" (0-31, 0-7: signal strength and channel bit error rate; 99 for unknown). See 3GPP 27007. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 message-storage\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 string\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Message storage memory type to enable for "SIM buffering". Possible values are: "SM" - SIM card memory or "ME" - Mobile equipment memory (may not be supported by your modem). check your modem's manual for more types. By default, if the option is not set, no message storage command will be sent to the modem and the modem's default message storage will be used (usually "SM"). \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 message-start\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 string\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Optional integer, defaults to 1. Specifies starting index in SIM buffer for new SMS. Most modems start numbering from 1, however a few like the UMG181 start numbering from 0. This parameter ensures that all SMS are fetched when using "SIM buffering". \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 enable-mms\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 boolean\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Optional, defaults to false. If enabled, Kannel would send an AT+CMMS=2 if it have more than one message on queue and hopefully will be quicker sending the messages. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 reset-string\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 string\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Which reset string to execute when \fs18\f2 max-error-count\fs20\f0  reached. Example for Falcom: AT+CFUN=1 \sa60\cell \row \pard\plain\sl-1\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb200\li960\sl260 \i\fs20\lang1033 A note about delivery reports and GSM modems:\i0  while it is possible (and supported) to receive delivery reports on GSM modems, it may not work for you. if you encounter problems, check that your modem's init string (if not the default) is set to correctly allow the modem to send delivery reports using unsolicited notification (check your modem's manual). If the init-string is not set as si, some modems will store delivery reports to SIM memory, to get at which you will need to enable sim-buffering. finally your GSM network provider may not support delivery reports to mobile units.\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb100\li960\sl260 \i About \fs18\f2 rawtcp\fs20\f0  mode:\i0  This mode allows you to use a GSM modem connected to a remote terminal server, such as Perle IOLAN DS1 or a Cisco router with reverse telnet. The teminal server should support raw TCP mode. The driver is not tested in telnet mode. It is recommended to use \fs18\f2 keepalive\fs20\f0  variable, in order to automatically reconnect in case of network connectivity problems.\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb200\s4\li960\sl312 {\*\bkmkstart _2602}{\*\bkmkend _2602}\b\fs24\lang1024\f1 Modem initialization\keepn\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb120\li960\sl260 \b0\fs20\lang1033\f0 This question has been asked frequently in the users mailing list. It usually comes in two forms: \hyphpar0\par\pard\sb100\li1320\sl260\fi-360 \tqr\tx1270\tx1320\tab 1.\tab Modem doesn't receive or transmit SMS.\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb100\li1320\sl260 In its current implementation, the at driver will panic if it cannot find the modem device and bearerbox won't start. This can happen either because the wrong modem device is configured or the device has no write access for kannel's user.\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb100\li1320\sl260 In the first case use system logs to discover where is your modem assigned to:\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb100\li1320\sl260 grep tty /var/log/messages\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb100\li1320\sl260 Then verify that this is indeed your GSM modem device by connecting to it with minicom or wvdial and issuing a few AT commands. Wvdial is preferrable, since it can also give you a working \fs18\f2 init-string\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb100\li1320\sl260 \fs20\f0 In the second case you need to give write access to kannel user. This is no problem if you run kannel as root, but it is not recommended to do so. In Ubuntu linux you just need to assign kannel user to group "dial". In other systems you can either:\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb100\li1320\sl234 \fs18\f2 chmod 666 /dev/modem\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb100\li1320\sl260 \fs20\f0 or preferably:\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb100\li1320\sl234 \fs18\f2 \sa0\par\fi0\sb0
chmod 664 /dev/modem\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
chgrp \i group\i0  /dev/modem\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
usermod -G \i group\i0  \i kannel-user\i0 \sa0\par\fi0\sb0
           \hyphpar0\par\pard\sb100\li1320\sl260\fi-360 \tqr\tx1270\tx1320\tab \fs20\f0 2.\tab Modem doesn't receive DLRs or SMS.\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb100\li1320\sl260 By default the modem doesn't know how to treat incoming messages. To tell it to send it to kannel you have to configure \fs18\f2 init-string\fs20\f0  with the \i +CNMI=x,x,x,x,x\i0  command. X's are decimal numbers and CNMI stands for Command New Message Indication. There is no hard rule about its values. They are model and manufacturer specific. Best to consult modem manual or manufacturer's web site. Failing that, wvdialconf might give a working CNMI. Finally see modems.conf for examples and try out different values. Some Nokia phones do not support this command, but are ready to transmit incoming messages from the start.\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb100\li1320\sl260 Since this setting is modem specific, kannel cannot understand what it means from its value, and if using unconventional values you should tell kannel through \fs18\f2 sim-buffering \fs20\f0 and \fs18\f2 message-storage\fs20\f0 . In any case it is useful to add +CMEE = 1 or 2 in the \fs18\f2 init-string\fs20\f0  in order to make the modem more verbose in its responses.\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb100\li1320\sl234 \fs18\f2 \sa0\par\fi0\sb0
group = modems\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
init-string = "AT+CNMI=2,3,0,1,0;+CMEE=1"\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
message-storage = ME or SM    Depending on your modem, you may need to adjust it\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
...\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
group = smsc\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
smsc = at\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
sim-buffering = true          This will tell kannel to search for messages in\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
...                           the modem (either memory or its SIM)\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
           \hyphpar0\par\pard\sb216\s3\li960\sl374 {\*\bkmkstart _2630}{\*\bkmkend _2630}\b\fs28\lang1024\f1 GSMA OneAPI v1.0 ParlayX SMS SOAP\keepn\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb144\li960\sl260 \b0\fs20\lang1033\f0 This implements the GSMA OneAPI v1.0 ParlayX SMS SOAP/XML interface in two flavors, the Ericsson SDP (service delivery platform) ParlayX and the GSMA OneAPI v1.0 SOAP interfaces.\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb100\li960\sl260 Example configuration for the Ericsson SDP variant:\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb200\li960\sl234 \fs18\lang1024\f2 \sa0\par\fi0\sb0
group = smsc\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
smsc = parlayx\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
system-type = ericsson-sdp\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
port = 10000\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
connect-allow-ip = 10.11.12.13\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
send-url = http://host/location\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
dlr-url = http://our-host:10000/dlr-location\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
smsc-username = tester\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
smsc-password = foobar\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
\sa200\par\trowd\trleft960\trhdr \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx3760\clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx6560\clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \b\fs20\f1 Variable\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \b\fs20\f1 Value\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \b\fs20\f1 Description\sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx3760\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx6560\clvertalb\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 system-type (m)\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 string\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Type of ParlayX connection. Currently supported are: 'oneapi-v1', 'ericsson-sdp'. The variants have the same ParlayX SOAP XML PDUs, but differ in the authentication scheme they use, where 'ericsson-sdp' uses WS-Security via wsse and 'oneapi-v1' uses plain HTTP basic authentication. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 port (m)\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 port-number\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Port number in which Kannel listens to (MO and DLR) messages from other SOAP service side. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 send-url (m)\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 url\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Location of the SOAP service to send MT messages. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 dlr-url (m)\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 url\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Location of our side SOAP service for DLR notifications. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 smsc-username (m)\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 string\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Username associated for the SOAP service connection. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 smsc-password (m)\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 string\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Password associated for the SOAP service username. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 use-ssl\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 boolean\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Defines whether listen port should use SSL. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 connect-allow-ip\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 IP-list\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  IPs allowed to use this SOAP service interface. If not set, "127.0.0.1" (localhost) is the only host allowed to connect. Typically you will allow the IP of the other side SOAP service here. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 window\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 boolean\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Number of concurrent sending threads. If not set, one thread is used. \sa60\cell \row \pard\plain\sl-1\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb216\s3\li960\sl374 {\*\bkmkstart _2697}{\*\bkmkend _2697}\b\fs28\f1 Fake SMSC\keepn\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb144\li960\sl260 \b0\fs20\lang1033\f0 Fake SMSC is a simple protocol to test out Kannel. It is not a real SMS center, and cannot be used to send or receive SMS messages from real phones. So, it is ONLY used for testing purposes.\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb200\li960\sl234 \fs18\lang1024\f2 \sa0\par\fi0\sb0
group = smsc\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
smsc = fake\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
port = 10000\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
connect-allow-ip = 127.0.0.1\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
\sa200\par\trowd\trleft960\trhdr \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx3760\clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx6560\clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \b\fs20\f1 Variable\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \b\fs20\f1 Value\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \b\fs20\f1 Description\sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx3760\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx6560\clvertalb\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 host (m)\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 hostname\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Machine that runs the SMSC. As IP (100.100.100.100) or hostname (their.machine.here) \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 port (m)\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 port-number\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Port number in smsc host machine \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 connect-allow-ip\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 IP-list\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  If set, only connections from these IP addresses are accepted. \sa60\cell \row \pard\plain\sl-1\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb216\s3\li960\sl374 {\*\bkmkstart _2727}{\*\bkmkend _2727}\b\fs28\f1 HTTP-based relay and content gateways\keepn\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb144\li960\sl260 \b0\fs20\lang1033\f0 This special "SMSC" is used for HTTP based connections with other gateways and various other relay services, when direct SMSC is not available.\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb200\li960\sl234 \fs18\lang1024\f2 \sa0\par\fi0\sb0
