\sa200\par\trowd\trleft960\trhdr \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx3760\clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx6560\clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \b\fs20\f1 Variable\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \b\fs20\f1 Value\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \b\fs20\f1 Description\sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx3760\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx6560\clvertalb\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 system-type (m)\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 string\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Type of HTTP connection. Currently supported are: 'kannel', 'brunet', 'xidris', 'clickatell' and 'generic'. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 send-url (m)\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 url\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Location to send MT messages. This URL is expanded by used system, if need to. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 no-sender\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 boolean\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Do not add variable sender to the send-url. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 no-coding\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 boolean\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Do not add variable coding to the send-url. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 no-sep\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 boolean\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Represent udh and text as a numeric string containing the hex-dump. For instance, text=%2b123 is represented as text=2b313233. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 port (m)\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 port-number\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Port number in which Kannel listens to (MO) messages from other gateway \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 use-ssl\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 boolean\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Defines whether listen port should use SSL. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 connect-allow-ip\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 IP-list\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  IPs allowed to use this interface. If not set, "127.0.0.1" (localhost) is the only host allowed to connect. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 smsc-username\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 string\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Username associated to connection, if needed. Kannel requires this, and it is the same as send-sms username at other end. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 smsc-password\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 string\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Password for username, if needed. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 max-pending-submits\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 number\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Optional the maximum number of outstanding (i.e. acknowledged) requests. As a guideline it is recommended that no more than 10 (default) requests are outstanding at any time. \sa60\cell \row \pard\plain\sl-1\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb200\s4\li960\sl312 {\*\bkmkstart _2805}{\*\bkmkend _2805}\b\f1 The "generic" system-type\keepn\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb120\li960\sl260 \b0\fs20\lang1033\f0 For a generic HTTP-based relay, the system-type 'generic' can be used. It can use the escape codes known from sms-service's get-url config directives in the send-url string to indicate the HTTP API calling style of the remote HTTP server, and the 3 HTTP body response parsing regular expressions 'status-success-regex' for successfull acknowledge, 'status-permfail-regex' for permanent failure and 'status-tempfail-regex' for temporary failure. It can also accomodate the incoming parameters and response codes and text. This system-type has a lot of extra parameters that gives it a lot of flexibility:\sa200\par\trowd\trleft960\trhdr \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx3760\clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx6560\clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \b\fs20\f1 Variable\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \b\fs20\f1 Value\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \b\fs20\f1 Description\sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx3760\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx6560\clvertalb\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 status-success-regex (o)\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 POSIX regular expression\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Regular expression to match against HTTP response body content, indicating a successful submission. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 status-permfail-regex (o)\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 POSIX regular expression\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Regular expression to match against HTTP response body content, indicating a permanent failure. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 status-tempfail-regex (o)\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 POSIX regular expression\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Regular expression to match against HTTP response body content, indicating a temporary failure. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 generic-foreign-id-regex (o)\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 POSIX regular expression\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Regular expression to match against HTTP response body content to get the foreign message id in case of successful submission. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 generic-param-username (o)\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 string\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Overrides the default parameter for the 'username' field used on incoming requests. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 generic-param-password (o)\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 string\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Overrides the default parameter for the 'password' field used on incoming requests. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 generic-param-from (o)\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 string\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Overrides the default parameter for the 'from' field used on incoming requests. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 generic-param-to (o)\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 string\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Overrides the default parameter for the 'to' field used on incoming requests. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 generic-param-text (o)\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 string\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Overrides the default parameter for the 'text' field used on incoming requests. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 generic-param-udh (o)\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 string\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Overrides the default parameter for the 'udh' field used on incoming requests. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 generic-param-service (o)\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 string\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Overrides the default parameter for the 'service' field used on incoming requests. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 generic-param-account (o)\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 string\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Overrides the default parameter for the 'account' field used on incoming requests. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 generic-param-binfo (o)\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 string\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Overrides the default parameter for the 'binfo' field used on incoming requests. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 generic-param-dlr-mask (o)\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 string\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Overrides the default parameter for the 'dlr-mask' field used on incoming requests. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 generic-param-dlr-err (o)\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 string\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Overrides the default parameter for the 'dlr-err' field used on incoming requests. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 generic-param-dlr-url (o)\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 string\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Overrides the default parameter for the 'dlr-url' field used on incoming requests. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 generic-param-dlr-mid (o)\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 string\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Overrides the default parameter for the 'dlr-mid' field used on incoming requests. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 generic-param-flash (o)\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 string\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Overrides the default parameter for the 'flash' field used on incoming requests. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 generic-param-mclass (o)\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 string\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Overrides the default parameter for the 'mclass' field used on incoming requests. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 generic-param-mwi (o)\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 string\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Overrides the default parameter for the 'mwi' field used on incoming requests. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 generic-param-coding (o)\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 string\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Overrides the default parameter for the 'coding' field used on incoming requests. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 generic-param-validity (o)\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 string\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Overrides the default parameter for the 'validity' field used on incoming requests. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 generic-param-deferred (o)\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 string\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Overrides the default parameter for the 'deferred' field used on incoming requests. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 generic-param-foreign-id (o)\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 string\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Overrides the default parameter for the 'foreign-id' field used on incoming requests. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 generic-param-meta-data (o)\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 string\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Overrides the default parameter for the 'meta-data' field used on incoming requests. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 generic-message-sent (o)\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 string\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  It allows you to set the text returned when a succesful request is made. If not set, defaults to 'Sent.'. Note that you can use all sms service escapes here, see {\field{\*\fldinst   HYPERLINK  \\l ID_escapecodes_46_title}{\fldrslt \i Parameters (Escape Codes)}} for details. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 generic-status-sent (o)\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 string\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Overrides the HTTP status code returned when a successful request is made. If not set, defaults to 202 (HTTP_ACCEPTED). \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\cellx3760\clvertalt\cellx6560\clvertalb\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 generic-status-error (o)\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 string\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Overrides the HTTP status code returned when a request is rejected for any reason. If not set, defaults to 202 (HTTP_ACCEPTED). \sa60\cell \row \pard\plain\sl-1\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb200\li960\sl260 \fs20\lang1033 An example for a 'generic' group looks like this:\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb200\li960\sl234 \fs18\lang1024\f2 \sa0\par\fi0\sb0
group = smsc\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
smsc = http\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
system-type = generic\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
port = 13015\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
send-url = "http://www.foobar.com/mt.php?from=%P&to=%p&text=%b"\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
status-success-regex = "ok"\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
status-permfail-regex = "failure"\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
status-tempfail-regex = "retry later"\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
generic-foreign-id-regex = "<id>(.+)</id>"\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
generic-param-from = "phoneNumber"\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
generic-param-to = "shortCode"\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
generic-message-sent = "Message sent with ID: %I"\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
generic-status-sent = 200\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
generic-status-error = 404\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb216\s3\li960\sl374 {\*\bkmkstart _2987}{\*\bkmkend _2987}\b\fs28\f1 Loopback SMSC (MT to MO direction switching)\keepn\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb144\li960\sl260 \b0\fs20\lang1033\f0 This special "SMSC" type can be used to route MT messages in bearerbox internally as MO input messages again. Therefore this tyoe is the MT wise counterpart of the 'reroute' functionality of the smsc group when MOs are re-routed as MTs.\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb200\li960\sl234 \fs18\lang1024\f2 \sa0\par\fi0\sb0
group = smsc\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
smsc = loopback\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
smsc-id = loop1\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
reroute-smsc-id = my_id\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
\sa200\par\trowd\trleft960\trhdr \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx3760\clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx6560\clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \b\fs20\f1 Variable\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \b\fs20\f1 Value\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \b\fs20\f1 Description\sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx3760\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx6560\clvertalb\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 reroute-smsc-id (o)\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs18\f2 string\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20  Tag the rerouted MO with the given value for smsc-id instead of the canonical smsc-id value of the smsc group itself. \sa60\cell \row \pard\plain\sl-1\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb216\s3\li960\sl374 {\*\bkmkstart _3005}{\*\bkmkend _3005}\b\fs28\f1 Using multiple SMS centers\keepn\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb144\li960\sl260 \b0\fs20\lang1033\f0 If you have several SMS center connections (multiple operators or a number of GSM modems) you need to configure one smsc group per SMS center (or GSM modem). When doing this, you might want to use routing systems to rout messages to specific centers - for example, you have 2 operator SMS centers, and the other is much faster and cheaper to use.\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb100\li960\sl260 To set up routing systems, first give an unique ID for each SMS center - or if you want to treat multiple ones completely identical, give them identical ID. Then use \fs18\f2 preferred-smsc-id\fs20\f0  and \fs18\f2 denied-smsc-id\fs20\f0  to set up the routing to your taste. See also SMS PUSH settings ('sendsms-user' groups), below.\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb216\s3\li960\sl374 {\*\bkmkstart _3011}{\*\bkmkend _3011}\b\fs28\lang1024\f1 Feature checklist\keepn\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb144\li960\sl260 \b0\fs20\lang1033\f0 Not all of Kannel's SMSC drivers support the same set of features. This is because they were written at different times, and new features are often only added to drivers that the feature author can test.\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb100\li960\sl260 The table in this section is an attempt to show exactly what features to expect from a driver, and to help identify areas where drivers need to be updated. Currently most of the entries are marked as "not tested" because the table is still new.\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb200\li960\sl260 {\*\bkmkstart _3015}{\*\bkmkend _3015}\b\lang1024 Table 7-2. SMSC driver features\sa100\keepn\par\trowd\trleft960\trhdr \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx1606\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx2252\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx2898\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx3544\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx4190\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx4836\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx5482\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx6128\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx6774\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx7420\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx8066\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx8712\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx9358 \plain