\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb216\s3\li960\sl374 {\*\bkmkstart _3636}{\*\bkmkend _3636}\b\fs28\lang1024\f1 PostgreSQL DLR storage\keepn\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb144\li960\sl260 \b0\fs20\lang1033\f0 To store DLR information into a PostgreSQL database you may use the \fs18\f2 dlr-storage = pgsql\fs20\f0  configuration directive in the \fs18\f2 core\fs20\f0  group.\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb100\li960\sl260 In addition to that you must have a \fs18\f2 dlr-db\fs20\f0  group defined that specifies the table field names that are used to the DLR attributes and a \fs18\f2 pgsql-connection\fs20\f0  group that defines the connection to the PostgreSQL server itself.\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb100\li960\sl260 Here is the example configuration: \hyphpar0\par\pard\sb200\li960\sl234 \fs18\f2 \sa0\par\fi0\sb0
group = pgsql-connection\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
id = mydlr\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
host = myhost.com\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
username = foo\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
password = bar\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
database = dlr\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
