\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb216\s3\li960\sl374 {\*\bkmkstart _3646}{\*\bkmkend _3646}\b\fs28\lang1024\f1 MS-SQL/Sybase DLR storage\keepn\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb144\li960\sl260 \b0\fs20\lang1033\f0 To store DLR information into a MS-SQL or Sybase (via FreeTDS) database you may use the \fs18\f2 dlr-storage = mssql\fs20\f0  configuration directive in the \fs18\f2 core\fs20\f0  group.\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb100\li960\sl260 In addition to that you must have a \fs18\f2 dlr-db\fs20\f0  group defined that specifies the table field names that are used to the DLR attributes and a \fs18\f2 mssql-connection\fs20\f0  group that defines the connection to the MS-SQL or Sybase server itself.\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb100\li960\sl260 Please note that the \fs18\f2 server\fs20\f0  configuration directive must match the corresponding \fs18\f2 [section]\fs20\f0  on \fs18\f2 freetds.conf\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb100\li960\sl260 \fs20\f0 Here is the example configuration: \hyphpar0\par\pard\sb200\li960\sl234 \fs18\f2 \sa0\par\fi0\sb0
group = mssql-connection\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
id = msdlr\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
server = myservername\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
username = foo\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
