              si-expires="2002-06-30T00:00:00Z">\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
    Want to test a fetch?\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
  </indication>\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
</si>\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
      \hyphpar0\par\pard\sb200\li960\sl260 \fs20\f0  Note that the date value of the si-expires attribute contains trailing zeroes. They are OK here, because SI tokenizer removes them. But phones does not accept them in the final SMS data message. You should probably use \fs18\f2 action="signal-high"\fs20\f0  for testing purposes, for it causes an immediate presentation of the push message. Production usage is a quite another matter.\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb100\li960\sl260 Another example of push content is Service Loading. In principle, the phone should fetch immediately content from URL \fs18\f2 http://wap.iobox.fi \fs20\f0 when it receives this document. This sounds quite insecure, and indeed, user invention is probably required before fetching. \hyphpar0\par\pard\sb200\li960\sl234 \fs18\f2 \sa0\par\fi0\sb0
